{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Moses said: Thus says YHWH: About midnight</b> — To Pharaoh he said this, and to his servants as well, as he said at the end of his words (Exodus 11:8): \"And all your servants these shall come down to me.\" He did not specify now on which night this plague would occur, for this statement and this declaration to Pharaoh took place before the first of the month of Nisan. And when he says <b>about midnight</b>, it would not be known which night it is. Behold, Moses did not inform them the night of their plague, but he said in anger: I will not continue to see your face, but you will call for me, and your servants will bow to me about midnight to depart from your land. And in the second section (Exodus 12:12) he specified to Israel: \"And I will pass through the land of Egypt on this night,\" and so on. And in the third section he said (Exodus 12:29): \"And it came to pass at midnight\" — the one mentioned, in which they performed the Pesach."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The phrase rendered \"about midnight\" translates כחצת הלילה, which Ramban quotes from the verse; he does not address the well-known Rabbinic issue of its precise sense."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:06:04.217232034Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}